WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.779
Speaker 1: We got a call from a viewer last
week who brought up China and a discussion

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:10.740
of the portrayal of China in American media.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.639
And during that conversation, during that
phone call, we talked about xenophobia towards

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:16.240
Asian-Americans over COVID.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.790
We talked about intellectual property theft
and a few other topics.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:24.680
And I got a very good email from Thomas over
the weekend, and Thomas said to me, You know,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.040
David, there is a China story to talk about,
but it's not really what the caller brought

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.340
up.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.340
Intellectual property theft.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.340
It's an issue.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.940
It's not the major geopolitical issue with
China.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.560
There's no real evidence that China intentionally
released COVID is bioweapon, so that's not

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.640
really like the big story with China.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.720
Yes, xenophobia against Asian-Americans for
real or perceived misdeeds by China is something

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:47.720
we should be against.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.740
We're not going to be xenophobic against Asian-Americans
because of something the Chinese government

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.440
did that that's happening, and that's bad.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.720
But Thomas wrote, there are real issues with
the Chinese Communist Party.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.860
Now that's another issue to clarify.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:04.570
The CCP and China, as in Chinese people, are
two different things.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:08.010
We're really talking about the Chinese government,
the Chinese Communist Party.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:12.740
And as Thomas wrote to me, there's a ton of
negativity towards China in general.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.490
That's very surface level.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.060
Some of it is based in plain old bigotry.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.880
Some of it is peddled by U.S. media.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:25.159
But there are many real reasons to be at odds
with the actions of the Chinese Communist

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:26.159
Party.

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:30.190
So let's look at the real concerns with the
Chinese government, the CCP.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.000
And these are not reasons to go to war with
China.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Caveat.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.460
I'm not suggesting war.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:39.470
I know that there's people possibly on the
revolutionary left who will see this segment

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.280
and say, I'm calling for another American
military intervention.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.229
No, the I'm not even saying these are reasons
to no longer trade with China.

00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:51.630
If we stop trading with China would be disastrous
for the American economy, as it's currently

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.640
set up.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.070
We're just going to talk about issues with
the Chinese government first.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:02.970
The ongoing Wiegert Genocide Wiggers are a
Muslim ethnic minority in China.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:07.659
China has been credibly accused of committing
crimes against humanity, possibly genocide

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:14.079
against the weaker population and other mostly
Muslim ethnic groups in the northwest region

00:02:14.079 --> 00:02:16.200
of Xinjiang.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:21.829
Leading human rights groups, including Amnesty
and Human Rights Watch, have put out reports

00:02:21.829 --> 00:02:25.419
accusing China of crimes against humanity
for their actions.

00:02:25.419 --> 00:02:27.360
There are reeducation camps.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.379
There are horrifying things and much has been
written about it.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:34.599
That's a real substantive issue with the Chinese
government.

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:37.099
Second, organ harvesting.

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:39.230
This is all that.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:44.870
If you put a positive spin on it, this is
oh, we get organ donations from prisoners

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.959
who have died of natural causes.

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:49.760
That's the story that China would tell.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:56.390
But a tribunal ruled in 2020 that China is
forcibly harvesting organs from prisoners,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:00.159
prisoners who certainly didn't volunteer to
donate organs.

00:03:00.159 --> 00:03:06.030
But it goes even further, possibly even prisoners
who are killed for organs not who have died

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.629
naturally.

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:12.329
The number of transplant centers in China
has gone up over 300 percent.

00:03:12.329 --> 00:03:14.659
Wait times for organs have come down dramatically.

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:19.969
It's not clear why China doesn't have much
in terms of an organized organ donation program.

00:03:19.969 --> 00:03:20.969
How is it happens?

00:03:20.969 --> 00:03:21.969
How does it happen?

00:03:21.969 --> 00:03:26.319
It seems this is a likely explanation, and
it is absolutely horrifying.

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:30.290
Note that back in 2012, a top Chinese official
said.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.909
China is going to phase out the practice of
taking organs from prisoners who have been

00:03:33.909 --> 00:03:39.779
executed as of 2020, we believe that that's
still going on even if it's not a side from

00:03:39.779 --> 00:03:41.359
executed.

00:03:41.359 --> 00:03:46.200
There's a lot of other ways that you can accelerate
the process of obtaining organs from prisoners.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.829
It seems that that's being done.

00:03:47.829 --> 00:03:48.900
Absolutely horrifying.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:55.870
Number three, China so poorly mismanaged its
own infrastructure that it likely has led

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.969
to hundreds or more Chinese people.

00:03:58.969 --> 00:04:04.110
It's hard to get real numbers from the CCP
to die due to flooding.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:08.519
And the idea here is that yes, there have
been heavy rainstorms that are not manmade,

00:04:08.519 --> 00:04:09.519
right?

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:14.559
Humans didn't make the rainstorms, but there
are serious allegations that the deaths are

00:04:14.559 --> 00:04:20.120
a result of this infrastructure madness craze
in China, where money is poured into projects

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.120
that look good sometimes generate returns
for people.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:29.570
But meanwhile, simple infrastructure that
could be improved to prevent senseless death

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:32.570
from heavy rains and people drowning are ignored.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:33.840
OK, complete mismanagement.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:40.010
That's a real criticism of what's being done
and then such corruption from the CCP that

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:45.820
causes all sorts of problems massive fraud,
embezzlement around these half finished villages

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:49.650
where people make a ton of money, the projects
are abandoned after the contracts in the cash

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:54.620
are handed out, as well as reconstruction
projects that never really happen, although

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:57.200
many people get rich from them.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:02.730
And then lastly, and this is a really big
deal of China's continued aggressive posturing

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:09.160
towards India, Taiwan and the South and East
China Seas more generally, each of which we've

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.820
talked about a little bit in the past.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:16.010
So on India, there have been somewhere between
four and 10 skirmishes of note between India

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:19.410
and China over the border, various face offs.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.970
We've talked about it a little bit on the
bonus show before the situation in the South

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:29.790
China Sea involving China, the Philippines
and Vietnam, where you see military activity

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:35.920
by China, naval maneuvers, other aggression
outposts being built concerning and then also

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:39.030
conflicts with Japan in the East China Sea.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:44.570
Other part of the sea it include it includes
Japan having scrambled jets in the past and

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.700
other escalation.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.520
So to be clear again, I want to be really
careful.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.740
I don't want war with China.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.260
I'm not saying invade China.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.670
I'm not saying the U.S. doesn't also do bad
things.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.430
Lots of countries exhibit this type of aggression.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:04.580
The difference is number one, a lot of the
criticisms of China in the U.S. media and

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.270
from, you know, people like Trump have been
very surface level and lead to xenophobia

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:12.850
against Asian Americans, which has no place
whatsoever.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.850
There are actual horrible things being done
by the Chinese government.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:22.130
Many countries that also want to do horrible
things don't have both the aggression and

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.470
the means to carry it out.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:30.120
The financial resources at their disposal,
the massive population that China has bigotry

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.950
against Asian-Americans because of this are
Chinese people.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.360
Anywhere is wrong and we're against it.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.880
I'm also not saying cut off China.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:42.750
From an economic standpoint, our economy is
now too inter intertwined with China.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:47.530
It would take a really long time to be able
to untangle that relationship without destroying

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.560
the American economy.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.050
So I'm not calling for that.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:54.830
But there are real geopolitical issues here
and humanitarian issues about which we should

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:55.830
be concerned.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:07:02.110
It's not bigotry to talk about that, and the
American media rarely touches these actual

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.550
issues.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.030
Let me know what you think.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:10.570
We'll have more on this story on the David
Pakman show Instagram, which you can find

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:10.810
at David Pakman show on Instagram.

